{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|prisma|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|πρίσμα||something sawed|tr=prisma|lang=grc}}, from {{term|πρίζειν||to saw|tr=prizein|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-prism.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|/pɹɪzm/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪzm}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|geometry|lang=en}} A [[polyhedron]] with [[parallel]] ends of the same size and shape, the other faces being [[parallelogram]]-shaped sides.
# A transparent block in the shape of a prism (typically with triangular ends), used to split or reflect light.
# A crystal in which the faces are parallel to the [[vertical]] [[axis]].

